<title>UK: BOE invites band 1,2 bills,monetary meet continues.</title>
<headline>BOE invites band 1,2 bills,monetary meet continues.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England invited UK money market operators to offer band 1 and 2 bills in exchange for cash to help alleviate a forecast 800 million stg liquidity shortage in the market.</p>
<p>The monthly monetary meeting was still going on at 1200 GMT, so it will not become clear until 1400 GMT at the earliest whether interest rates have been changed.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
